From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenFuse contributors <openfuse@invalid>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:30:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ALSA: usb-audio: Meter MiniFuse playback in the PCM path

The Arturia MiniFuse does not meter the audio it plays, and an application
that opens the card's hw: device directly bypasses the sound server, so
userspace has no place to measure it. The driver sees every sample it
sends, so hand the outgoing data of each playback URB to the MiniFuse
quirk, which keeps the peak per channel and exposes it as a read-only
"Playback Level Meter" control.

Only plain PCM URBs of the MiniFuse 2 (1c75:af90) are passed on; the
quirk ignores formats other than S16_LE, S24_3LE and S32_LE.

Signed-off-by: OpenFuse contributors <openfuse@invalid>
---
 sound/usb/pcm.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/usb/pcm.c b/sound/usb/pcm.c
--- a/sound/usb/pcm.c
+++ b/sound/usb/pcm.c
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@
 #include "power.h"
 #include "media.h"
 #include "implicit.h"
+#include "mixer_minifuse.h"
 
 #define SUBSTREAM_FLAG_DATA_EP_STARTED	0
 #define SUBSTREAM_FLAG_SYNC_EP_STARTED	1
@@ -1613,6 +1614,13 @@
 			else
 				bytes = copy_to_urb_quirk(subs, urb, stride, bytes);
 			/* bytes is now amount of outgoing data */
+			if (!subs->tx_length_quirk &&
+			    subs->stream->chip->usb_id == USB_ID(0x1c75, 0xaf90))
+				snd_minifuse_playback_tap(subs->stream->chip,
+							  urb->transfer_buffer,
+							  bytes,
+							  subs->cur_audiofmt->channels,
+							  ep->cur_format);
 		}
 
 		subs->last_frame_number = usb_get_current_frame_number(subs->dev);
